  "worked_solution": "Our goal is to write the equation in the form \n\n$$\nax+by=c,\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b,$ and $c$ are integers with no common factors and $a\\ge 0.$\n\nWe begin by moving all of the variables to the left-hand side and all of the constants to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-3x+7 \\\\ 3x+y & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $a,b,$ and $c$ are integers with no common factors, and $a\\ge 0.$ So, we are done!\n\nThe standard form of the line is \n\n$$\n3x+y=7.\n$$",
